{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-d73daed3f3a135a26d3f","statement":"Let $\\bfA\\in \\alg(\\lincat)$. Suppose the product $m: \\bfA\\otimes\\bfA\\to\\bfA$ admits an $\\bfA\\otimes\\bfA^{\\rev}$-linear right adjoint $m^R$. Then the following statements hold.\n\n- For every $\\bfA$-module $\\bfM$, the continuous right adjoint of $\\mathrm{act}_\\bfM$ exists and is given by\n\n\\[\n\\bfM\\xrightarrow{(m^R\\circ \\mathbf{1}_\\bfA)\\otimes\\id_\\bfM} \\bfA\\otimes \\bfA\\otimes \\bfM \\xrightarrow{\\id_\\bfA\\otimes \\mathrm{act}_\\bfM}\\bfA\\otimes \\bfM.\n\\]\n\nIn particular, the Beck-Chevalley map $ (\\id_\\bfA\\otimes F)\\circ \\mathrm{act}_{\\bfM}^R\\to  \\mathrm{act}_{\\bfN}^R\\circ F$ associated to $F\\circ \\mathrm{act}_\\bfM\\cong \\mathrm{act}_\\bfN\\circ (\\id_\\bfA\\otimes F)$ is an isomorphism.\n\n- Every (op)lax $\\bfA$-linear functor between $\\bfA$-module categories is $\\bfA$-linear.\nConsequently, if $F:\\bfM\\to \\bfN$ is an $\\bfA$-linear functor between $\\bfA$-module categories, with a continuous right adjoint $F^R$ (resp. a left adjoint $F^L$), then $F^R$ (resp. $F^L$) is $\\bfA$-linear.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"c86747d3b2d0991936e46d25909796f6514689d5d0b3758ebb970c9bd373d445","kind":"lemma","label":"Lemma 447","ref_key":"lem-rigid-lax-is-strict","name":"","order":630,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":13168,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":973,"math_hints":119}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined th